 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "과거진행형 was / were + -ing",
   "en": "past continuous: was / were + -ing"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "과거의 어느 순간에 진행 중이던 일은 was / were + 동사-ing로 말합니다. I / he / she / it에는 was, we / you / they에는 were를 씁니다. 부정은 wasn't / weren't, 질문은 was / were를 앞으로 보냅니다.",
   "en": "Use was / were + verb-ing for an action in progress at a moment in the past. Use was with I / he / she / it and were with we / you / they. Negative: wasn't / weren't. For questions put was / were first."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "긍정 / positive",
     "I was sleeping. They were waiting."
    ],
    [
     "부정 / negative",
     "She wasn't cooking. We weren't talking."
    ],
    [
     "질문 / question",
     "Were you listening? Yes, I was."
    ],
    [
     "시간 / time",
     "At eight last night I was doing my homework."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "과거의 한 시점에 하고 있던 일에 씁니다.",
    "en": "Use it for what was in progress at a past moment."
   },
   {
    "ko": "I / he / she / it에는 was, we / you / they에는 were.",
    "en": "was for I / he / she / it; were for we / you / they."
   },
   {
    "ko": "동사 -ing: cook → cooking, make → making, run → running.",
    "en": "Verb-ing spelling: cook → cooking, make → making, run → running."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
